1. What was your primary contribution to the project?

I developed the C program, including temperature monitoring, configurable ranges, average calculations, file saving, and test cases.

2. What was the most challenging technical problem your team encountered?

The biggest challenge was compiling the code because the online compiler did not support the Raspberry Pi’s pigpio library.

3. How did your team use testing or debugging to solve a problem?

We tested different temperature inputs, checked the expected outputs, and used simulation to debug the program before running it on the Raspberry Pi.

4. Which skills from CSE 1106 were most useful?

Learning how to use GitHub properly, program the Raspberry Pi, and work with PowerShell was especially useful.

5. What would you improve if you had more time?

I would add a more user-friendly interface, automatic temperature sensors, and timestamps for saved readings.
